  "narrative": {
    "northStar": "The Welcome Desk",
    "overview": "NEXTORA should feel like a kind person at an arrivals desk who hands you the right form, in your language, and tells you plainly what to do next. The world is ink on warm paper: a deep Harbour Ink for authority and calm, a single warm Desert Clay for progress and encouragement, and a paper-white ground that keeps every screen quiet enough to read when you are tired and reading in a second language.\n\nDensity is moderate and list-shaped. Screens are a single column of flat, bordered cards inside a 640px reading frame, each card one task or one fact, with a 44px touch target on everything that responds. Personality comes from restraint and honesty rather than decoration: one dark ink hero panel per screen at most, one shape-only illustration (a rising sun over a skyline of plain blocks, with small circles for people gathering), and no photography.\n\nThe system carries 16 languages in their own scripts, including right-to-left Arabic and Urdu. Every visual decision has to survive a line that is twice as long in Malayalam, or mirrored in Urdu.",
    "keyCharacteristics": [
      "Ink on warm paper: Harbour Ink and Desert Clay over a paper-white ground.",
      "Flat at rest: depth from borders and tonal fills, not shadows.",
      "One column, one task per card, 640px maximum reading width.",
      "Noto Sans in every script, three weights only.",
      "A floating pill tab bar whose active \"drop\" springs to the selected tab.",
      "Honest states: review tags, \"AI-generated\" labels and empty states are first-class visual elements."
    ],
    "rules": [
      {
        "name": "The Two Voices Rule",
        "body": "Ink means \"act / this is official\"; clay means \"you made progress\". Do not swap them: a primary button is never clay, and a completed state is never ink.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The AA Floor Rule",
        "body": "Every text pair must pass WCAG AA (4.5:1 body, 3:1 large). When clay or ink is needed as text on a ground where it fails, use its `-text` or `-on-dark` variant instead.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Right Font For The Script Rule",
        "body": "Text is always rendered through the `T` component, which picks the Noto family for the language on screen and aligns right in RTL. Official names (for example \"UAE PASS\") stay in Latin Noto Sans inside every language.",
        "section": "typography"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Three Weights Rule",
        "body": "Only 400, 600 and 700 are loaded. Do not ask for 300, 500 or 800.",
        "section": "typography"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Flat Desk Rule",
        "body": "Cards are separated by borders and spacing, never by drop shadows. Press feedback is a slight shrink (scale 0.985) and fade (opacity 0.92), not a lift.",
        "section": "elevation"
      }
    ],
    "dos": [
      "Do take every colour from `theme/index.ts` (and the matching gluestack variables) and refer to them by role.",
      "Do keep every pressable at least 44px in both directions, including text links.",
      "Do render all text through `T` so the right Noto family and reading direction apply, and flip directional icons in RTL.",
      "Do keep screens to one column inside the 640px frame, with one task or fact per card.",
      "Do show honesty states visually: review tags on content, an \"AI-generated, may be wrong\" label on assistant answers, and the Empty component (ink-soft icon well plus Slate text) instead of placeholder content.",
      "Do re-check contrast when you add a text pair, and keep `docs/CONTRAST.md` in step with the current palette."
    ],
    "donts": [
      "Don't add drop shadows to cards; depth is borders and tonal fills. The Ask NEXTORA voice card is the only exception.",
      "Don't use Desert Clay for primary actions, or Harbour Ink for completion.",
      "Don't use photography or people imagery; illustration stays shape-only.",
      "Don't add a second typeface; Noto Sans in each script is the only family.",
      "Don't hard-code colours in screens. Translucent fills are tokens too: `accentOnDarkSoft` (trust strip on ink), `glassOnDark` (dark tab pill) and `scrim` (behind sheets).",
      "Don't bring back the retired names `aubergine`, `purple`, `teal`, `navy` or `offWhite`. The palette is `ink`, `night`, `paper` and `clay`; tag tones and avatar hues are `ink` and `clay`.",
      "Don't design a dark theme from the gluestack `dark` variables; they are unused boilerplate. Dark appears only as the ink hero."
    ]
  }
}
